                <pb facs="0479" n="467" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg467"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/7089: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">Then in France, to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">St.
                                Jean de Luz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-20T12:00:00+00:00">December 20,
                        1937—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received December 20—10:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>417. Conversation with one in position to know corroborates the general report of
                    a serious anti-Franco conspiracy to remove him by assassination. Important
                    papers and money reported missing from Salamanca. Many arrests reported. Closing
                    of frontiers associated <pb facs="0480" n="468" xml:id="pg468"/> with
                    disappearance of papers. Identity of conspirators carefully guarded but believed
                    to be the Falange or [omission?] army officers.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
